<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!--
Alabama Appellate Courts - Events API Response
===============================================

This XSD documents the JSON API response structure from the Alabama
appellate courts events endpoint (calendar/oral arguments).

API Endpoint:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/cms/events

Query Parameters:
- startDateFrom: ISO 8601 datetime with timezone (e.g., "2026-01-21T00:00:00.001-06:00")
- startDateTo: ISO 8601 datetime with timezone (e.g., "2026-02-21T23:59:59.900-06:00")
- page: Page number (0-indexed)
- size: Results per page (default: 100)
- sort: Sort field and direction (e.g., "startDate,desc")

Response Format: JSON

The response contains calendar events (oral argument sessions) with pagination.
Each event has a UUID that can be used to fetch the cases/hearings for that session.

Example Response Structure:
{
    "_embedded": {
        "results": [
            {
                "eventUUID": "f6f1c3a9-f43e-4bdf-8963-8438198b3243",
                "eventName": "Oral Argument",
                "eventStatusTypeID": "380000",
                "suppressCalendarAssignmentFlag": false,
                "courtID": "1",
                "courtAbbreviation": "Alabama Supreme Court",
                "courtSessionType": "Oral Argument",
                "panelFlag": true,
                "startDate": "2026-02-04T06:00:00.000+00:00",
                "location": "Heflin-Torbert Judicial Building"
            },
            {
                "eventUUID": "abc123...",
                "eventName": "Oral Argument",
                "courtID": "2",
                "courtAbbreviation": "Alabama Court of Civil Appeals",
                "courtSessionType": "Oral Argument",
                "startDate": "2026-01-28T06:00:00.000+00:00",
                "location": ""
            }
        ]
    },
    "page": {
        "size": 100,
        "totalElements": 3,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "number": 0
    }
}

Event Fields:
- eventUUID: Unique identifier for the event/session (required for fetching hearings)
- eventName: Name of the event (usually "Oral Argument")
- courtID: Numeric court identifier (1=Supreme, 2=Civil, 3=Criminal)
- courtAbbreviation: Full court name (use to map to court_id)
- courtSessionType: Type of session (e.g., "Oral Argument")
- startDate: Event start date/time (ISO 8601)
- location: Physical location (e.g., "Heflin-Torbert Judicial Building")
- panelFlag: Boolean indicating if this is a panel session

Court Abbreviation Mapping:
- "Alabama Supreme Court" -> court_id: "ala"
- "Alabama Court of Civil Appeals" -> court_id: "alactapp"
- "Alabama Court of Criminal Appeals" -> court_id: "alacrimapp"

Data Extraction:
- event_uuid: From eventUUID
- court_id: Mapped from courtAbbreviation
- event_date: Parsed from startDate (extract date portion)
- location: From location field

Filtering:
- Filter by court_id if specified in search params
- Filter by date range (event_date must be within start_date and end_date)

Pagination:
- Process all pages until totalPages is reached
- Use page number from response to fetch next page

Next Step:
After parsing each event, fetch the hearings (cases) for that event:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/events/{event-uuid}/hearings

Source URL Pattern:
Events don't have individual detail pages - they're only visible in search results
-->

<xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
        This is a documentation-only XSD for the Alabama Events API.
        The actual response is JSON, not XML.
    </xs:documentation>
</xs:annotation>

</xs:schema>
